<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">problem:
<br class="ltx_break"/></span>The real numbers <math alttext="a,b,c,d" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S7.SS1.p5.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c,d</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy simultaneously the equations
<math alttext="abc-d=1,bcd-a=2,cda-b=3,dab-c=-6" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S7.SS1.p5.m2"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">abc-d=1,bcd-a=2,cda-b=3,dab-c=-6</annotation></semantics></math>.
Prove that <math alttext="a+b+c+d\neq 0" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="S7.SS1.p5.m3"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+c+d\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
